  "_moves_doc": [
    "`moves` re-homes ONE declaration by name. Everything below the first entry is",
    "there for one reason: a module's LOAD-TIME statements may only read values from",
    "modules that are guaranteed to have evaluated first, and in ES modules that",
    "guarantee only exists outside the importer's strongly-connected component. The",
    "sim<->ui function cycle puts ~42 modules in one SCC, so the handful of values a",
    "load-time statement reads across a module boundary are moved into modules that",
    "sit OUTSIDE it (world.js and ui/dom.js are leaves — zero imports). Function",
    "bindings are exempt: ESM instantiates them at link time, before any evaluation.",
    "`analyze`/`check` prove this — they compute the real ESM evaluation order and",
    "fail on any load-time read that would land before its owner module evaluated."
  ],
  "moves": {
